{"diagnosis": "Loopback send 0xa5 never set recv_buf_valid, causing `TRAP: uart timeout, no byte received` and `FAIL 0xdead` instead of a received byte. Expected recv_divcnt to increment each cycle to exceed cfg_divider and advance recv_state 1->2 and 10->0, but line 74 does `recv_divcnt <= recv_divcnt + 0` so the counter stays 0 and reception never completes. Root cause is the zero increment in picosoc/simpleuart.v line 74 stalling the UART receiver divider.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picosoc/simpleuart.v b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
--- a/picosoc/simpleuart.v
+++ b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
@@ -66,11 +66,11 @@
 	always @(posedge clk) begin
 		if (!resetn) begin
 			recv_state <= 0;
 			recv_divcnt <= 0;
 			recv_pattern <= 0;
 			recv_buf_data <= 0;
 			recv_buf_valid <= 0;
 		end else begin
-			recv_divcnt <= recv_divcnt + 0;
+			recv_divcnt <= recv_divcnt + 1;
 			if (reg_dat_re)
 				recv_buf_valid <= 0;
", "expected": "tohost PASS, loopback byte 0xa5 received with no uart timeout"}

